coffee:
  # NOTE (luolita 0.1.4): bridged data must be single-line valid JSON.
  rules = [{ "text": "Exactly one action per invocation: --run a.js --eval 1 is an error." }, { "text": "No bare subcommands / positional actions: winterjs2 a.js is an error — write winterjs2 --run a.js. Only script arguments go after --: winterjs2 --run app.js -- --port 8080." }, { "text": "Modifiers belong to their action: --port only works with --serve, --filter only with --test, --watch with --test/--run/--serve, --schema only with --config, --allow-* only with --run/--eval/--test/--repl. Mismatches exit 1." }]

template:
  h1 winterjs2 Quickstart
  blockquote 5-minute path from zero to running JavaScript. 中文版见 #[a(href='#/zh/quickstart') 快速上手].
  h2 1. Install &amp; verify
  pre
    code.
      $ cargo build
      $ export SDKROOT="$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)"          # macOS, needed every new shell
      $ export LIBCLANG_PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib"
      $ export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:$PATH"
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --eval '40 + 2'            # → 42
  h2 2. Run a file, evaluate code, start a REPL
  pre
    code.
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --run sample/web/timers.js  # run a file, print completion value
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --eval 'await Promise.resolve(7)'  # → 7
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --repl                       # interactive REPL (Ctrl-D to exit)
  p Rules (see #[a(href='#/en/cli') CLI reference]):
  ul
    each r in rules
      li= r.text
  h2 REPL cheat sheet
  pre
    code.
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2                       # bare start also enters the REPL
      ❄&gt; WinterJS2. + Tab                           # complete WinterJS2.* with a doc pane
      ❄&gt; .doc WinterJS2.fs.readFile                 # full doc page for any topic
      ❄&gt; await fetch("data:text/plain,hi").then((r) => r.text())  # top-level await works
      ❄&gt; .help / .exit                             # help, quit (.quit, exit(), Ctrl-D too)
  p Tab shows a completion menu with a documentation pane on the right; unclosed brackets keep reading (multiline); Ctrl-C twice within 2s quits.
  h2 3. Use Node APIs and Web globals
  pre
    code.
      // hello.mjs — ESM, Web globals and node: imports both work
      import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
      import path from 'node:path';

      const text = readFileSync(new URL('./hello.mjs', import.meta.url), 'utf8');
      console.log('self bytes:', new TextEncoder().encode(text).length);
      console.log('join:', path.join('a', 'b'));
      const res = await fetch('data:text/plain,hi');
      console.log(await res.text()); // hi
  pre
    code.
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --run hello.mjs
  p CommonJS also works (#[code require], #[code module.exports], #[code __dirname]).
  h2 4. Run tests, lint, format, serve
  pre
    code.
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --test sample/test-runner/   # discover + run test files
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --test sample/test-runner/ --filter 'basics*'
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --test sample/test-runner/ --watch   # re-run on change (Ctrl-C to stop)
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --lint -- --help              # forwarded to oxlint verbatim
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --fmt                         # forwarded to oxfmt
      $ ./target/debug/winterjs2 --serve sample/serve-hello/public --port 8080 \
          --handler sample/serve-hello/handler.mjs            # static + dynamic fetch + WS
  h2 5. Next steps
  ul
    li #[a(href='#/en/api') API reference] — every module, stability, and known deviations.
    li #[a(href='#/en/cli') CLI reference] — full flag reference with action scope.
    li #[code sample/&lt;area&gt;/*.js] — 128 runnable examples, one per module.
